From 478f3d75b9558c62360111e73a39f6a428918d88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UNI-OFFICE Engineer <engineer@unioffice.local>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:26:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approvals): make decisions atomic

A pending approval could transition more than once. approve() and reject()
read the request, checked that it was still pending, then issued an
unconditional update. Two concurrent deciders both passed the read check and
both wrote, producing pending -> approved -> rejected and running the task,
work and event side effects twice.

Complete the conditional transition that was declared on ApprovalRepository
but never implemented, restoring the workspace to a compiling state:

- SupabaseApprovalRepository.resolvePending performs the decision as a single
  statement guarded on status = 'pending', so Postgres row locking admits
  exactly one decider.
- WorkApprovalService claims the transition before any side effect and raises
  ApprovalConflictError when another actor already won.
- The API maps that conflict to 409 INVALID_STATE instead of a 500.

Adds a concurrency test that fails against the previous implementation.
